From 20e020a98f55679572ad7d18e1c4897b9951a1b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MT6762 local experiment <mt6762-build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:40:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm: add explicit read-only MSDC file-backed laboratory

AI-assisted local experiment, not intended for upstream submission. Model only inherited polled CMD8/CMD13/CMD17 state and read real raw backend sectors without storage writes. Include admission, completion, metadata, locking and file-length failure tests.
---
 docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst           |  31 +++
 hw/arm/mt6762.c                      |  92 ++++++++-
 hw/misc/meson.build                  |   2 +-
 hw/misc/mt6762_msdc_lab.c            | 283 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/hw/misc/mt6762_msdc_lab.h    |  33 ++++
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_msdc.py        | 202 +++++++++++++++++++
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_msdc_inputs.py |  64 ++++++
 7 files changed, 704 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hw/misc/mt6762_msdc_lab.c
 create mode 100644 include/hw/misc/mt6762_msdc_lab.h
 create mode 100644 tests/mt6762/test_lab_msdc.py
 create mode 100644 tests/mt6762/test_lab_msdc_inputs.py

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
index 8d09ee5..6cec12f 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
@@ -293,3 +293,34 @@ checks. Eight-core and single-core native build17 runs missed the default
 READY-low transition and correctly rejected the raw pair; the explicit
 2000us fixture subsequently exercised successful raw-pair acquisition.
 Neither timing establishes physical PMIC behavior.
+
+Explicit read-only MSDC file-backed fixture
+------------------------------------------
+
+``lab-msdc=on`` and a nonempty ``lab-msdc-image=/path/to/raw`` must be selected
+together. The file must already exist, be regular, and contain complete512-byte
+sectors. Its actual file length must match the raw BlockBackend length; image
+format probing, writable backends and shared writers are excluded. This is a
+synthetic inherited-state controller/card fixture with real file payloads,
+not a complete eMMC device, a stock-Linux storage implementation or a physical
+card initialization sequence.
+
+The fixture maps MSDC0 at0x11230000 and exposes fixed CFG0x89/SDC_CFG0x20000,
+RCA1 and read-only synthetic EXT_CSD with actual backing capacity, user area,
+CMDQ disabled, eight-bit bus, HS200 timing and CARD_TYPE0x56. Only CMD13,
+CMD8/SEND_EXT_CSD and CMD17 single-sector reads are accepted. Interrupts are
+polled; DMA and physical IRQ delivery are not modeled. Reset, clock, tuning,
+DMA, crypto and card data writes are rejected. Native tests must independently
+validate their inherited ownership/configuration contract before issuing reads.
+
+``lab-msdc-fault`` supplies busy/queue/crypto/stale-interrupt admission faults,
+command/data CRC or timeout, short/missing completion, stuck acknowledgement,
+wrongR1, backend error and individual EXT_CSD metadata mismatches. Read-only
+``lab-msdc-state`` exposes command, FIFO, completion and backend-attempt counts.
+Clearing a model fault does not repair a native driver's latched fault state.
+``test_lab_msdc.py`` checks actual file bytes, metadata, errors and default
+absence. ``test_lab_msdc_inputs.py`` checks regular/whole-sector file admission,
+shared-writer exclusion and unchanged source hashes. The initial rounded
+513-byte file acceptance was corrected using actual stat size plus backend
+length equality before the successful input suite. No test image or phone
+firmware is included in these source patches.
